/-!
# The level of a lattice

Let `L` be a lattice in a real inner product space `E`, with dual lattice `L^∨ = ZLattice.dual L`.
The *level* of `L` is the least positive integer `N` such that `N ‖x‖² / 2` is an integer for every
`x ∈ L^∨` (`ZLattice.level`). For an even lattice it is the order of the discriminant quadratic form
`q_L(x + L) = ‖x‖² / 2 mod ℤ` on the discriminant group `A_L = L^∨ ⧸ L`, and it is the level `N`
of the congruence subgroup `Γ₀(N)` governing the transformation law of the theta series of `L`
(of weight `n / 2`, `n` the rank, with a character or multiplier system depending on `L`).

The integers `N` with `N ‖x‖² ∈ 2ℤ` for all `x ∈ L^∨` form a subgroup of `ℤ`, and the level
generates it: `level L ∣ N` exactly when `N` has this property (`ZLattice.level_dvd_iff`). This
characterization holds for every lattice, since the level is defined as an unguarded infimum; no
statement here depends on its value when no positive `N` works. That does not happen for a full
integral lattice (`ZLattice.IsIntegral.level_pos`): there the order `d` of the finite group `A_L`
kills `A_L`, so `d x ∈ L` and `d ‖x‖² = ⟪x, d x⟫ ∈ ℤ` for `x ∈ L^∨`, and `level L ∣ 2 d`. By
polarization the level also controls the dual inclusion of a full lattice, `level L • L^∨ ≤ L`, so
the exponent of `A_L` divides the level and `|A_L|` divides `level L ^ n`, `n` the rank, since
`A_L` is generated by `n` elements (`ZLattice.rank_discriminantGroup_le`). For an integral lattice
`|A_L| = det L`, so every prime dividing `det L` divides the level. The same characterization
computes the level of an orthogonal direct sum: the dual of `L ⊕ M` is `L^∨ ⊕ M^∨` and squared
norms add, so `level (L ⊕ M) = lcm (level L) (level M)` (`ZLattice.level_orthSum`).

The level is neither the exponent of `A_L` nor `det L`. For an orthonormal basis `b` of a nonzero
space and a positive integer `m`, the scaled cubic lattice `√m • ℤ b` has level `2 m`
(`ZLattice.level_sqrt_smul_span_orthonormalBasis`): its dual is `(√m)⁻¹ • ℤ b`, with squared norms
`‖y‖² / m`. Thus `√2 ℤ ⊆ ℝ`, which is even with `A_L ≅ ℤ/2` and `det L = 2`, has level `4`
(`ZLattice.level_span_sqrt_two`), and so has `√2 ℤ²`, with `A_L ≅ (ℤ/2)²` and `det L = 4`; the
odd unimodular lattice `ℤⁿ` has level `2`. For an even lattice,
`level L = 1` exactly when `L` is unimodular (`ZLattice.IsEven.level_eq_one_iff`). Evenness is
needed for this: the lattice `½ ℤ ⊆ ℝ` has the even dual `2 ℤ`, so it has level one, but it is
neither even nor unimodular.

This is the level of the real model of a lattice, with the norm of `E` as its quadratic form. The
rational model `TauCeti.IntegralLattice` has the analogous invariant
`TauCeti.IntegralLattice.level`, defined by the same condition on its dual lattice, and this file
follows its API. For a full integral lattice the two agree on the rational model
`ZLattice.ratModel` (`ZLattice.level_ratModel`), which transports the descriptions proved there.
Conversely the real model `TauCeti.IntegralLattice.realModel` of a positive definite rational
lattice `M` has the level of `M` (`TauCeti.IntegralLattice.level_realModel`), so the levels computed
on the rational side, such as those of the root lattices, hold verbatim for their real models.
For even `L` the level divides `N` exactly when `N` kills the discriminant quadratic form
(`TauCeti.IntegralLattice.IsEven.level_dvd_iff`). For a `ℤ`-basis `b` of `L` with real Gram matrix
`G = (⟪b i, b j⟫)`, the level divides `N` exactly when `N • G⁻¹` is an integral matrix with even
diagonal (`ZLattice.level_dvd_iff_gram`), so it is the least `N > 0` with this property
(`ZLattice.isLeast_level`). Indeed `G⁻¹` is the Gram matrix of the basis of `L^∨` dual to `b`.

The approach and API here (the unguarded-infimum definition, the divisibility characterization,
the dual inclusion and the discriminant-group bounds) are adapted from the earlier formalization
by tauceti-ai-for-science in
[Tau Ceti PR #20694](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/pull/20694).

## Main definitions

* `ZLattice.level L`: the least `N > 0` with `N ‖x‖² / 2 ∈ ℤ` for every `x ∈ L^∨`.

## Main statements

* `ZLattice.level_dvd_iff`: `level L ∣ N` if and only if `N ‖x‖² ∈ 2ℤ` for every `x ∈ L^∨`.
* `ZLattice.level_dvd_two_mul_card_discriminantGroup`, `ZLattice.IsIntegral.level_pos`: the level
  divides `2 |A_L|`, which is `2 det L` for a full integral lattice, and is then positive.
* `ZLattice.level_nsmul_mem`: `level L • x ∈ L` for `x ∈ L^∨`.
* `ZLattice.exponent_discriminantGroup_dvd_level`: the exponent of `A_L` divides the level.
* `ZLattice.card_discriminantGroup_dvd_level_pow`: for a full lattice `|A_L|` divides
  `level L ^ n`, and `ZLattice.prime_dvd_level`: every prime dividing `|A_L|` divides the level.
* `ZLattice.IsEven.level_eq_one_iff`: an even lattice has level one exactly when it is unimodular.
* `ZLattice.level_comap`: the level is invariant under linear isometry equivalences.
* `ZLattice.level_orthSum`: the level of an orthogonal direct sum `L ⊕ M` is
  `lcm (level L) (level M)`.
* `ZLattice.level_ratModel`: the level of a full integral lattice is the level of its rational
  model, and `TauCeti.IntegralLattice.level_realModel`: the level of the real model of a positive
  definite rational lattice is the level of that lattice.
* `ZLattice.level_dvd_iff_gram`, `ZLattice.isLeast_level`: for a full integral lattice with a
  `ℤ`-basis of real Gram matrix `G`, the level is the least `N > 0` for which `N • G⁻¹` is an
  integral matrix with even diagonal.
* `ZLattice.level_sqrt_smul_span_orthonormalBasis`: the lattice `√m • ℤⁿ`, `n > 0`, has level `2 m`.

## References

* W. Ebeling, *Lattices and Codes*, 3rd ed., Springer, 2013, Chapter 3.
* H. Iwaniec, *Topics in Classical Automorphic Forms*, AMS, 1997, Chapter 10.
-/

public section

open Module Submodule
open scoped Pointwise RealInnerProductSpace TensorProduct

namespace ZLattice

variable {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F]

/-- The level of a lattice `L`: the least `N > 0` such that `N ‖x‖² / 2` is an integer for every
`x` in the dual lattice. For an even lattice this is the order of the discriminant quadratic form
`‖x‖² / 2 mod ℤ` on `L^∨ ⧸ L`. The definition is the unguarded infimum, so it has a value on every
lattice; `level_dvd_iff` characterizes it in general, and `IsIntegral.level_pos` shows that it is
positive for a full integral lattice. -/
noncomputable def level (L : Submodule ℤ E) : ℕ :=
  sInf {N : ℕ | 0 < N ∧ ∀ x ∈ dual L, ∃ m : ℤ, (N : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ 2 = 2 * m}

variable {L : Submodule ℤ E}

/-- For `x` in the dual lattice, `level L * ‖x‖²` is an even integer. -/
theorem exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq {x : E} (hx : x ∈ dual L) :
    ∃ m : ℤ, (level L : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ 2 = 2 * m := by
  rcases (level L).eq_zero_or_pos with h | h
  · exact ⟨0, by simp [h]⟩
  -- A positive infimum is attained, so the level itself lies in the defining set.
  rw [level] at h ⊢
  exact (Nat.sInf_mem (Nat.nonempty_of_pos_sInf h)).2 x hx

/-- The level generates the subgroup of integers `N` with `N ‖x‖² ∈ 2ℤ` for every `x ∈ L^∨`:
`level L ∣ N` exactly when `N ‖x‖² / 2` is an integer for every `x` in the dual lattice. -/
theorem level_dvd_iff {N : ℕ} :
    level L ∣ N ↔ ∀ x ∈ dual L, ∃ m : ℤ, (N : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ 2 = 2 * m := by
  refine ⟨?_, fun hN ↦ ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨k, rfl⟩ x hx
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hx
    exact ⟨m * k, by push_cast; rw [mul_comm (level L : ℝ), mul_assoc, hm]; ring⟩
  rcases N.eq_zero_or_pos with rfl | hN0
  · exact dvd_zero _
  -- The remainder of `N` modulo the level has the same property, and is smaller than the level.
  have hpos : 0 < level L := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h ↦ by
    rw [level, Nat.sInf_eq_zero] at h
    rcases h with h | h
    · exact lt_irrefl 0 h.1
    · exact Set.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.mp h N ⟨hN0, hN⟩
  refine Nat.dvd_of_mod_eq_zero (Nat.eq_zero_of_not_pos fun hr ↦ ?_)
  refine (Nat.mod_lt N hpos).not_ge ?_
  conv_lhs => rw [level]
  refine Nat.sInf_le ⟨hr, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hN x hx
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hx
  -- `N % level L = N - level L * q` is an integer combination of `N` and the level.
  have hmod : ((N % level L : ℕ) : ℝ) = N - level L * (N / level L : ℕ) := by
    rw [eq_sub_iff_add_eq]
    exact_mod_cast Nat.mod_add_div N (level L)
  refine ⟨a - b * (N / level L : ℕ), ?_⟩
  rw [hmod, Int.cast_sub, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_natCast]
  linear_combination ha - ((N / level L : ℕ) : ℝ) * hb

/-- The level is invariant under linear isometry equivalences. -/
@[simp]
theorem level_comap (e : F ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] E) :
    level (ZLattice.comap ℝ L e.toLinearEquiv.toLinearMap) = level L := by
  refine Nat.dvd_antisymm (level_dvd_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_) (level_dvd_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_)
  · rw [dual_comap] at hx
    simpa using exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hx
  · simpa using exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq (L := ZLattice.comap ℝ L e.toLinearEquiv.toLinearMap)
      (x := e.symm x) (by simpa [dual_comap] using hx)

/-- The level of an orthogonal direct sum is the least common multiple of the levels of the
summands. -/
@[simp]
theorem level_orthSum (L : Submodule ℤ E) (M : Submodule ℤ F) :
    level (orthSum L M) = (level L).lcm (level M) := by
  refine eq_of_forall_dvd fun N ↦ ?_
  simp only [Nat.lcm_dvd_iff, level_dvd_iff, dual_orthSum, mem_orthSum]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨fun x hx ↦ ?_, fun y hy ↦ ?_⟩, fun ⟨hL, hM⟩ z hz ↦ ?_⟩
  · simpa [WithLp.prod_norm_sq_eq_of_L2] using h (WithLp.toLp 2 (x, 0)) (by simpa using hx)
  · simpa [WithLp.prod_norm_sq_eq_of_L2] using h (WithLp.toLp 2 (0, y)) (by simpa using hy)
  · obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hL _ hz.1
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hM _ hz.2
    exact ⟨a + b, by rw [WithLp.prod_norm_sq_eq_of_L2, mul_add, ha, hb]; push_cast; ring⟩

/-- The level of a lattice divides twice the order of its discriminant group
`L^∨ ⧸ (L ∩ L^∨)`, which is `det L` for a full integral lattice. When the discriminant group is
infinite its `Nat.card` is `0`, and the statement is trivial. -/
theorem level_dvd_two_mul_card_discriminantGroup :
    level L ∣ 2 * Nat.card (DiscriminantGroup L) := by
  refine level_dvd_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_
  -- The order `d` of the discriminant group kills the class of `x`, so `d • x ∈ L` and
  -- `d ‖x‖² = ⟪x, d • x⟫` is an integer.
  have hd : Nat.card (DiscriminantGroup L) • x ∈ L := by
    have := card_nsmul_eq_zero' (G := DiscriminantGroup L)
      (x := Submodule.Quotient.mk (⟨x, hx⟩ : dual L))
    rwa [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, discriminantGroup_mk_eq_zero_iff] at this
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := mem_dual.mp hx _ hd
  refine ⟨m, ?_⟩
  rw [← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul ℝ, real_inner_smul_right, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq] at hm
  push_cast
  linear_combination 2 * hm

/-! ### Full lattices -/

section FiniteDimensional

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [DiscreteTopology L] [IsZLattice ℝ L]

/-- The level controls the dual inclusion: `level L • x ∈ L` for every `x ∈ L^∨`, that is,
`level L • L^∨ ≤ L`. -/
theorem level_nsmul_mem {x : E} (hx : x ∈ dual L) : level L • x ∈ L := by
  suffices level L • x ∈ dual (dual L) by rwa [dual_dual] at this
  refine mem_dual.mpr fun y hy ↦ ?_
  -- Polarization: `2 N ⟪x, y⟫ = N ‖x + y‖² - N ‖x‖² - N ‖y‖²` is twice an integer.
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hx
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hy
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq (add_mem hx hy)
  refine ⟨c - a - b, ?_⟩
  rw [← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul ℝ, real_inner_smul_left]
  push_cast
  linear_combination (hc - ha - hb - (level L : ℝ) * norm_add_sq_real x y) / 2

/-- The exponent of the discriminant group divides the level. -/
theorem exponent_discriminantGroup_dvd_level :
    AddMonoid.exponent (DiscriminantGroup L) ∣ level L := by
  refine AddMonoid.exponent_dvd_iff_forall_nsmul_eq_zero.mpr fun a ↦ ?_
  induction a using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with | _ x
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, discriminantGroup_mk_eq_zero_iff]
  exact level_nsmul_mem x.2

/-- A full integral lattice has positive level. -/
theorem IsIntegral.level_pos (h : IsIntegral L) : 0 < level L := by
  borelize E
  have := h.finite_discriminantGroup
  exact Nat.pos_of_dvd_of_pos level_dvd_two_mul_card_discriminantGroup
    (Nat.mul_pos two_pos Nat.card_pos)

/-- The order of the discriminant group of a full lattice of rank `n` divides `level L ^ n`. For an
integral lattice this order is `det L`. -/
theorem card_discriminantGroup_dvd_level_pow :
    Nat.card (DiscriminantGroup L) ∣ level L ^ finrank ℝ E :=
  (card_dvd_exponent_nsmul_rank' (DiscriminantGroup L) fun a ↦
    AddMonoid.exponent_dvd_iff_forall_nsmul_eq_zero.mp exponent_discriminantGroup_dvd_level
      a).trans (pow_dvd_pow _ rank_discriminantGroup_le)

/-- Every prime dividing the order of the discriminant group of a full lattice divides its level.
For an integral lattice this order is `det L`. -/
theorem prime_dvd_level {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hpd : p ∣ Nat.card (DiscriminantGroup L)) :
    p ∣ level L :=
  hp.dvd_of_dvd_pow (hpd.trans card_discriminantGroup_dvd_level_pow)

/-- An even full lattice has level one exactly when it is unimodular. -/
theorem IsEven.level_eq_one_iff (h : IsEven L) : level L = 1 ↔ IsUnimodular L := by
  refine ⟨fun h1 ↦ h.isIntegral.isUnimodular_iff.mpr ?_, fun hu ↦ Nat.dvd_one.mp ?_⟩
  · -- At level one the dual lattice is even, hence integral, so it lies in its own dual `L`.
    have hdual : IsEven (dual L) := isEven_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ by
      simpa [h1] using exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq hx
    simpa using isIntegral_iff_le_dual.mp hdual.isIntegral
  · refine level_dvd_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_
    simpa using isEven_iff.mp h x (hu.dual_eq ▸ hx)

/-! ### The rational model -/

/-- The level of a full integral lattice is the level of its rational model. -/
@[simp]
theorem level_ratModel (hL : IsIntegral L) : (ratModel hL).level = level L := by
  -- On the rational model the norm of `x` is `‖ratModelMap L x‖²`, and `ratModelMap` carries the
  -- dual carrier onto `L^∨`, so the two divisibility conditions on `N` coincide.
  have hnorm (x : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] L) : ((ratModel hL).norm x : ℝ) = ‖ratModelMap L x‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [TauCeti.IntegralLattice.norm_apply, ratModel_form_cast, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]
  refine Nat.dvd_antisymm (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp
    (((ratModel hL).level_dvd_iff _).mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_)) (level_dvd_iff.mpr fun y hy ↦ ?_)
  · obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq ((mem_ratModel_dualCarrier_iff hL x).mp hx)
    refine ⟨m, Rat.cast_injective (α := ℝ) ?_⟩
    push_cast
    rw [hnorm, hm]
  · obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := exists_ratModelMap_eq_of_mem_dual hL hy
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := ((ratModel hL).level_dvd_iff _).mp dvd_rfl x
      ((mem_ratModel_dualCarrier_iff hL x).mpr hy)
    refine ⟨m, ?_⟩
    rw [← hnorm]
    exact_mod_cast hm

/-- **The level in a basis.** For a full integral lattice `L` with a `ℤ`-basis `b` of real Gram
matrix `G = (⟪b i, b j⟫)`, the level divides `N` exactly when `N • G⁻¹` is an integral matrix with
even diagonal. -/
theorem level_dvd_iff_gram (hL : IsIntegral L) {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (b : Basis ι ℤ L) (N : ℕ) :
    level L ∣ N ↔ ∃ M : Matrix ι ι ℤ, (∀ i, Even (M i i)) ∧
      M.map (Int.cast : ℤ → ℝ) = (N : ℝ) • (Matrix.gram ℝ fun i ↦ (b i : E))⁻¹ := by
  -- Transport `b` to a carrier basis of the rational model, whose integral Gram matrix, cast to
  -- `ℝ`, is the real Gram matrix of `b`; the inverse may then be taken over `ℚ`.
  have hgram : Matrix.gram ℝ (fun i ↦ (b i : E)) =
      (((ratModel hL).gramMatrix (b.map (ratModelCarrierEquiv hL))).map
        (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ)).map (Rat.castHom ℝ) := by
    ext i j
    simp [Matrix.gram_apply, hL.integralForm_cast]
  rw [← level_ratModel hL, ← Int.natCast_dvd_natCast,
    (ratModel hL).level_dvd_iff_gramMatrix (b.map (ratModelCarrierEquiv hL)) N, hgram,
    ← Matrix.map_nonsing_inv]
  refine exists_congr fun M ↦ and_congr_right fun _ ↦ ?_
  rw [← (Matrix.map_injective (Rat.castHom ℝ).injective).eq_iff, Matrix.map_map]
  simp [← Matrix.ext_iff]

/-- **The level as a least element.** For a full integral lattice `L` with a `ℤ`-basis `b` of real
Gram matrix `G = (⟪b i, b j⟫)`, the level is the least `N > 0` for which `N • G⁻¹` is an integral
matrix with even diagonal. -/
theorem isLeast_level (hL : IsIntegral L) {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (b : Basis ι ℤ L) :
    IsLeast {N : ℕ | 0 < N ∧ ∃ M : Matrix ι ι ℤ, (∀ i, Even (M i i)) ∧
      M.map (Int.cast : ℤ → ℝ) = (N : ℝ) • (Matrix.gram ℝ fun i ↦ (b i : E))⁻¹} (level L) :=
  ⟨⟨hL.level_pos, (level_dvd_iff_gram hL b _).mp dvd_rfl⟩,
    fun _ ⟨hN, hM⟩ ↦ Nat.le_of_dvd hN ((level_dvd_iff_gram hL b _).mpr hM)⟩

end FiniteDimensional

/-! ### Scaled cubic lattices -/

/-- For an orthonormal basis `b` of a nonzero space and a positive integer `m`, the scaled cubic
lattice `√m • ℤ b` has level `2 m`: its dual `(√m)⁻¹ • ℤ b` has squared norms `‖y‖² / m` with
`‖y‖² ∈ ℤ`, attaining `1 / m`. For `m = 2` and rank `2` this is the level `4` of `√2 ℤ²`, whose
determinant is also `4` but whose discriminant group `(ℤ/2)²` has exponent `2`. -/
theorem level_sqrt_smul_span_orthonormalBasis {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [Nonempty ι]
    (b : OrthonormalBasis ι ℝ E) {m : ℕ} (hm : m ≠ 0) :
    level (√(m : ℝ) • span ℤ (Set.range b)) = 2 * m := by
  have hs : 0 < √(m : ℝ) := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (by positivity)
  have hsq : √(m : ℝ) ^ 2 = m := Real.sq_sqrt (Nat.cast_nonneg m)
  have hnorm (y : E) : ‖(√(m : ℝ))⁻¹ • y‖ ^ 2 = ‖y‖ ^ 2 / m := by
    rw [norm_smul, mul_pow, norm_inv, Real.norm_of_nonneg hs.le, inv_pow, hsq, inv_mul_eq_div]
  have hdual : dual (√(m : ℝ) • span ℤ (Set.range b)) = (√(m : ℝ))⁻¹ • span ℤ (Set.range b) := by
    rw [dual_smul _ hs.ne', dual_span_orthonormalBasis]
  refine Nat.dvd_antisymm (level_dvd_iff.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_) ?_
  · -- Every vector of the dual is `(√m)⁻¹ • y` with `y ∈ ℤ b`, so `‖y‖²` is an integer.
    rw [hdual, mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists] at hx
    obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := isIntegral_iff.mp (isUnimodular_span_orthonormalBasis b).isIntegral y hy y hy
    refine ⟨k, ?_⟩
    rw [hnorm, ← real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, hk]
    push_cast
    field_simp
  · -- The vector `(√m)⁻¹ • b i` of the dual has squared norm `1 / m`.
    obtain ⟨i⟩ := ‹Nonempty ι›
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := exists_level_mul_norm_sq_eq (L := √(m : ℝ) • span ℤ (Set.range b))
      (x := (√(m : ℝ))⁻¹ • b i)
      (hdual ▸ smul_mem_pointwise_smul _ _ _ (subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩))
    rw [hnorm, b.orthonormal.1 i, one_pow] at hk
    have h : (level (√(m : ℝ) • span ℤ (Set.range b)) : ℝ) = 2 * m * k := by
      field_simp at hk
      linarith
    exact Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp ⟨k, by exact_mod_cast h⟩

/-- The lattice `√2 ℤ ⊆ ℝ` has level `4`, although its determinant is `2` and its discriminant
group `(1 / √2) ℤ ⧸ √2 ℤ` has exponent `2`. -/
theorem level_span_sqrt_two : level (span ℤ {√2} : Submodule ℤ ℝ) = 4 := by
  simpa [smul_span] using
    level_sqrt_smul_span_orthonormalBasis (OrthonormalBasis.singleton Unit ℝ) two_ne_zero

end ZLattice

/-! ### The real model of a rational lattice -/

namespace TauCeti.IntegralLattice

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V] (M : IntegralLattice V) (hM : M.IsPosDef)

/-- The real model of a positive definite rational lattice `M` has the level of `M`. -/
@[simp]
theorem level_realModel : ZLattice.level (M.realModel hM) = M.level :=
  (ZLattice.level_ratModel (M.isIntegral_realModel hM)).symm.trans
    (M.ratModelRealModelIsometry hM).level_eq.symm

end TauCeti.IntegralLattice
